.TH SCALE 1 "2025" "ChonkOS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
scale \- resource and size inspection
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scale
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.I command
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B scale
prints sorted tables (largest first, limited to \fB\-\-top\fR rows) of memory,
boot, package, or directory usage.
Exit status is 0 on success and non-zero on error.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-json
Print machine-readable JSON on stdout instead of a table.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR ram " [\fB\-\-top\fR N]"
Top processes by PSS (from /proc/<pid>/smaps_rollup), plus ZRAM statistics
from /sys/block/zram0/mm_stat. Default N=10. JSON unit: bytes.
.TP
.BR boot " [\fB\-\-top\fR N]"
Boot time per unit from systemd-analyze blame. Default N=10. JSON unit: ms.
.TP
.BR pkg " [\fB\-\-top\fR N]"
Installed packages by installed size, tagged [manual] or [auto] per
apt-mark showmanual. Default N=15. JSON unit: bytes.
.TP
.BR dir " [\fIpath\fR] [\fB\-\-top\fR N]"
Sizes of immediate subdirectories of \fIpath\fR (default .). Refuses /proc,
/sys, /dev. Default N=15. JSON unit: bytes.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
scale ram --top 20
.TP
scale --json boot
.TP
scale pkg --top 30
.TP
scale dir /var/log
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR chonk (1)
